  "title": "The Map Shop",
  "summary": "Paul segue as instruções, encontra a pequena loja na esquina e compra um mapa para continuar sua jornada.",
  "audio_url": "/audios/book-20.mp3",
  "word_count_target": 140,
  "story_en": "Paul reaches the corner and turns left. Ahead, he spots a small shop with a large clean window. Over the door, a wooden sign reads: City Books and Maps.\n\nHe pushes the door and steps inside. A quiet bell rings. An elderly clerk stands behind the wooden counter, reading a newspaper.\n\n“Good morning,” the clerk greets him with a kind voice. “Can I help you find something?”\n\n“Good morning,” Paul replies. “I am looking for a road map of the region.”\n\nThe clerk nods and pulls out a large paper map from a shelf. “This one shows every town, mountain, and path clearly.”\n\n“How much does it cost?” Paul asks.\n\n“It is ten dollars,” the clerk answers.\n\nPaul opens his bag, takes out the money, and pays for the item. With the map in his hands, Paul feels confident about the road ahead.",
